+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+Every tool registered on `ToolRegistry` in `src/orchestration/tools/registry.ts` declares a JSON Schema `inputSchema` that is sent to the model provider, and `ToolRegistry.execute` enforces that same schema against `input` before invoking the tool's executor. Validation turns malformed model tool calls into recoverable `ToolResponse` values rather than letting unvalidated payloads reach the executor or aborting the conversation turn.
+
+## Schema compilation and per-call resolution
+
+- `ToolRegistry.register` compiles a static tool definition's `inputSchema` at registration time and throws an error naming the tool when the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at registration time naming the tool when a static inputSchema cannot be compiled](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L99)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` resolves per call and validates `input` against the `inputSchema` returned for that call rather than a stale schema from an earlier call ([validated by: validates a function-valued tool definition against the schema returned for each call rather than a stale one](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L114)).
+
+## Execution-time validation and error contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` enforces `required`, declared types and `enum` before calling the executor, returning a `ToolResponse` naming the failing property on rejection while passing valid input — including unlisted extra properties, without type coercion or injected defaults — through to the executor unchanged ([validated by: rejects input violating required or enum without calling the executor, while passing valid extra keys through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L13)).
+- Rejection results and log lines name the failing property paths and failed constraints (including expected types) without ever exposing any property value from the rejected payload ([validated by: names the failing field and expected type on a type mismatch without exposing input values in the result or logs](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L53)).
+- Because a schema rejection returns a `ToolResponse` rather than throwing, `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` delivers the rejection message to the provider as a `tool_result` on the next round so the model can correct its call and resolve the turn ([validated by: returns a validation failure as a tool_result so the next orchestrator round can correct the call and resolve](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L150)).
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` throws an error only when the requested tool name is unregistered (`Unknown tool: <name>`), never when a registered tool's `inputSchema` rejects `input`.
